[ti:Day 07]

[00:00.00]clientele 例 How do you approach this potential clientele to maximise your earning at the end of the month? 在月末你怎样挖掘你的潜在客户 从而使自己的收入最大化？
[00:13.69]crash 例 According to their views, the mortgage market and the housing market would surely crash. 按照他们的观点，抵押贷款市场和住房市 场肯定会崩溃。
[00:26.29]contribute 例 The important thing is to give everyone a chance to contribute their ideas and know that they have been heard. 重要的是给每个人一 个贡献想法并知道他们的意见已为人所知的机 会。
[00:42.16]care 例 We care not just for how well off we are today but how well off we will be in the future. 我们关心的不仅仅是我们目前的生活多么富足， 还包括我们未来的生活。
[00:53.67]blank 例 As I learned the news of my mother's illness, my mind went completely blank. 当我知 道妈妈生病的消息时，大脑一片空白。
[01:04.41]solidarity 例 The situation raises the question about solidarity among members of the board. 该情
[01:16.54]mainstream 例 It surely is not the mainstream technology in wide use at present. 很明显，现在它还不是 一项被广泛使用的主流技术。
[01:26.81]cable 例 Under the deal, Microsoft succeeds in introducing its recently-launched cable television software into millions of homes in the UK. 在这笔交易中，微软公司成功地将其新发 布的有线电视软件推向数以百万计的英国家庭。
[01:45.32]collective 例 Whether or not you agree with that somewhat extreme opinion, collective intelligence will continue to be a big driver of web innovation. 无论你是否赞同这种有些极端的 观点，集体智慧都将继续成为网络创新的巨大驱 动力。
[02:04.93]fragment 例 Do not let the discussion fragment into a desultory conversation with no clear direction. 别让讨论变得支离破碎，成为没有明确方向的漫 谈。
[02:18.15]lax 例 The subcommi t tee claimed that the authorities were lax in investigating most of the cases. 小组委员会声称当局在调查大部分案 件时不够严格。
[02:30.75]greeter 例 You can tell the greeter that you are expecting a customer. 你可以告诉接待员你正在 等一位客户。
[02:39.62]consortium 例 They have recently formed a consortium of textile manufacturers. 最近他们组成了一家纺织 联营企业。
[02:50.04]bribery 例 The Siemens af fair also shows how far Europe still lags behind America in prosecuting bribery. 西门子事件也表明欧洲在贿 赂起诉方面仍落后美国很多。
[03:03.73]current 例 The current recession has had a huge impact on the personal savings rate. 最近的经 济萧条对个人储蓄率有相当大的影响。
[03:14.47]homogeneous 例 Calling two events by the same name does not make them homogeneous. 用同一名称命名 两个事件并不会让它们同质化。
[03:25.05]cooperate 例 Mr. White had promised to cooperate with us, but he cried off at the last minute. 怀特先 生本来答应与我们合作，但在最后一刻打了退堂 鼓。
[03:36.87]chaos 例 The financial world, as a creator of wealth, had accumulated so much risk for years that it plunged us into chaos. 多年来，作为财富创造 者的金融界已积累了如此多的风险，致使我们陷 入混乱之中。
[03:52.43]germane 例 He asked some questions that are germane and central to the issue. 他问了一些与议题密切 相关的问题。
[04:02.23]equivalent 例 The fiscal deficit was the equivalent of incurring a loss of 3 million dollars a day throughout 2013. 财政赤字造成的损失相当于 2013年全年每天损失300万美元。
[04:17.01]cook 例 Let's hope he didn't cook the books of the company. 让我们祈祷他没有篡改公司的账本吧。
[04:24.32]pose 例 The measure will pose a serious limitation to the growth of service-oriented enterprises. 该举措会对服务型企业的发展造成严重的限制。
[04:37.08]gravity 例 We completely understand the gravity of the global economic crisis. 我们完全明白全球性 经济危机的严重性。
[04:47.35]expectation 例 The performance of these new employees is quite beyond my expectation. 这些新员工的 表现大大超出我的预期。
[04:58.55]champion 例 With constant practice and training, you hone your body, your mind and your heart, and then gain the intuition and reflexes of a champion. 经过持续的练习和训练，你的身体和 心智会得到磨炼，从而具备冠军的直觉和反应 力。
[05:17.84]contender 例 He was a contender for the Democratic presidential nomination in 2004. 他在2004年是 民主党总统提名的一名竞争者。
[05:28.73]adman 例 Peter looks not at all like a typical adman. 彼得看起来不像个典型的广告商。
[05:35.26]paradox 例 It's a paradox that drinking a lot of water often makes you feel thirsty. 真不可思议，你喝 那么多的水反而常常觉得口渴。
[05:45.84]tumble 例 The spot gold market underwent a sharp tumble. 现货黄金市场惨遭严重的价格下跌。
[05:53.00]allocate 例 My company plans to allocate more resources to the technical department. 我公司 计划给技术部门划拨更多的资源。
[06:04.05]spot 例 The advertisement is spotted at eight minutes past five every evening. 那个广告被安 排在每天傍晚5点零8分播放。
[06:14.16]evaluate 例 To evaluate the new proposal, we need to do a lot of market research. 为评估新提案，我 们需要做大量的市场调研。
[06:24.27]magnify 例 The government decided to use bank loans to magnify domestic buying power. 政府决定用 银行贷款增强国内购买力。
[06:35.32]incorporate 例 We have to incorporate the company for some financial reasons. 由于一些财务上的原 因，我们不得不将公司合并。
[06:45.43]fluctuate 例 Banks usually need to be much more cautious about business lending as commodity prices fluctuate far more than property prices. 通常银行要对商业贷款更为谨慎，因为商品价格 的波动比房地产价格大得多。
[07:03.79]envisage 例 I never envisaged spending my whole life in a foreign country. 我从未想过要在异国度过一 生。
[07:13.28]habitual 例 His boss discharged him for habitual absenteeism. 他因习惯性旷工而被老板解雇了。
[07:21.37]assortment 例 We notice that you have changed the assortment on this contract. 我们注意到你在这 份合同中更改了分类。
[07:31.48]diversify 例 The investors can diversify while making the most of any economic recovery. 投资者可 以充分利用每一次经济复苏，从事多种经营活 动。
[07:42.99]cap 例 The company's cash growth in one quarter was higher than the market cap of many companies. 这个公司一个季度的现金增长量超过 了很多公司的市值。
[07:55.28]customs 例 The customs figures show a steady decline in British trade. 海关数字表明英国的贸易一直在 走下坡路。
[08:04.31]prosper 例 With the advent of the new manager, the company began to prosper. 随着新经理的到来, 公司业务开始有了起色。
[08:13.95]churn 例 The travel agency not only lost money but also faced the loss of repeat business through customer churn. 那家旅行社不仅损失了钱财， 还遭遇了因客户流失而造成的回头生意的减少。
[08:28.42]gross 例 Deductions are the amounts subtracted by the company from your gross payroll. 扣除费用 是公司从你的工资总额中扣留的部分。
[08:39.62]nascent 例 The nascent system reform of the hospital didn't have the intended effect. 初期的医院体 制改革并没有取得预期效果。
[08:50.67]vintage 例 The trusts are not up and running yet. 这些 信托基金尚未到位运营。
